<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00N2">Notation <span data-tag="00N2">2.4.7.3</span> <span class="named">(Lengths)</span>.</a> Let $(W,S)$ be a Coxeter system. Then the group $W$ is generated by $S$: that is, every element of $W$ can be written as a product of elements of $S$. For each $w \in W$, we let $\ell (w)$ denote the smallest nonnegative integer $n$ for which $w$ factors as a product $s_1 s_2 \cdots s_ n$, where each $s_ i$ belongs to $S$. We will refer to $\ell (w)$ as the <em>length</em> of $w$. </p>
